abstract: >-
  Software and aggregate results for the JAMIA manuscript "Future-Information
  Leakage in 30-Day Readmission Prediction: An Empirical Audit and a
  Calibrated Electronic Health Record Model in Medicare-Insured Adults".
  Versions v7 to v15 remove a prior-utilization feature (los_trend_180d) and
  two derived interactions that encoded later admissions, rebuild the feature
  table from the raw MIMIC-IV tables without global imputation and with
  discharge and documentation-time cutoffs, and rerun the complete pipeline;
  all earlier releases report inflated performance (see
  LEAKAGE_CORRECTION_v7.md). Contains the leakage-safe staged recursive
  feature elimination pipeline, the empirical first-admission leakage test,
  the final 44-feature XGBoost model (src/pipeline_v13; document builders in
  src/pipeline_v15), canonical machine-readable results
  (results_v13/final_model_v13.json and companions), and figures.
  Out-of-fold AUROC of the complete selection procedure 0.7057 (95% CI
  0.7016 to 0.7102, primary); test AUROC 0.7056 (95% CI 0.6964 to 0.7145) on
  the historically exposed test partition, calibration slope 0.990.
  Same-cohort baselines: LACE 0.605 and HOSPITAL 0.647. MIMIC-IV row-level
  data are not included, per the PhysioNet Credentialed Health Data Use
  Agreement.
keywords:
